    {
      "name": "Markdown",
      "tileType": "MARKDOWN",
      "configured": true,
      "bounds": {
        "top": 494,
        "left": 1672,
        "width": 380,
        "height": 570
      },
      "tileFilter": {},
      "isAutoRefreshDisabled": false,
      "markdown": "\n# Resources waste 💵🔴\nWe're looking for two conditions:\n1. **Memory usage, % of limit** > 70%\n2. **CPU usage, % of limit** < 70%\n\nCondition 1 tells us that the pod has been assigned a limit (check memory limit, bytes) higher than the utilization.\nCondition 2 tells us the CPU usage utilization compared the assigned limit.\n\n\nFor example, a node with 17.29%\nof **memory usage, % of the limit**, and a memory limit assigned of 5GB, means that we can re-adjust the limit to 1.33GB for the pod to perform at 70% of memory utilization. Last column is the recommended memory limit to assign to the pod based on the real utilization to the application\n\nThank you OneAgent! \n\n### Next action? \n\nChange your yaml files to improve the utilization of resources of your cloud providers and see those changes in real time \n\n💵⚡"
    },
    {
      "name": "Markdown",
      "tileType": "MARKDOWN",
      "configured": true,
      "bounds": {
        "top": 1064,
        "left": 1672,
        "width": 380,
        "height": 1102
      },
      "tileFilter": {},
      "isAutoRefreshDisabled": false,
      "markdown": "# Column Values Explained \n\n\n### Memory Requests\nThe sum of the memory requests of the pods of the workload, as defined in the specifications.\n\n### Memory Limits\nThe sum of the memory requests of the pods of the workload, as defined in the specifications.\n\n### Memory Usage vs. Limits\nThe memory all processes inside the workloads are using divided by the memory limit defined for the workload, in percentage.\n\n### CPU Requests\nThe sum of the CPU requests of the pods of the workload, as defined in the specifications.\n\n### CPU Limits\nThe sum of the CPU limits of the pods of the workload, as defined in the specifications.\n\n### CPU Usage vs. Limits\nThe CPU all processes inside the workloads are using divided by the CPU limit defined for the workload, in percentage.\n\n### Recommended Memory Limit\nThe memory limit that has to be set so that the memory usage is 70% of the memory limit.\n\n### Recommended CPU Limit\nThe CPU limit that has to be set so that the CPU usage is 70% of the CPU limit.\n\n#### Ref. [Resource Management for Pods and Containers - Kubernetes official documentation](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/manage-resources-containers/) "
    },
